\label{prop:upgrade}
Let $H$ be the defining ideal of $s$ generic points in $\mathbb P^N$ over base field of arbitrary characteristic. Assume
\begin{equation}\label{eq:genericgap}
N\widehat\alpha(H)>\operatorname{reg}(H)+N-1.
\end{equation}
Then there exists a nonempty dense Zariski-open subset $U\subset\mathcal P_{N,s}$ such that, for every $X\in U$ and every $r\ge1$,
$$
I_X^{(Nr)}\subseteq \mathfrak m^{r(N-1)}I_X^r.
$$
